  <title>4.17.4: Geometric Recursive Definitions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01164</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.17.4: Geometric Recursive Definitions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>e5d40348-a4db-499d-bfe6-33783aed6af6</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down (5 minutes)</title>
<title>Student Activity</title>
<para>The geometric sequence \(G\) starts 12, 6, . . .</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>
    Write a recursive definition for sequence \(G\).
  </item>
  <item>
    Sketch a graph representing the first 5 terms of sequence \(G\).
  </item>
</list>
<title>Student Response</title>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>
    \(g(1)=12,g(n)=0.5⋅g(n−1)\) for \(n\geq2\) or equivalent.
  </item>
</list>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>
    <figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/39aa8bce7a8bf396638bb5e8190604457882cd9c"/></media></figure></item>
</list>
<title>Response to Student Thinking</title>
<title>Points to Emphasize</title>
<para>If students still struggle, plan to spend more time on the launch to 7.2.</para></section>
</content>
